<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62644" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεύκ-η</span></b> , ἡ, a cutaneous
		disease, so called from its colour: a kind of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leprosy</i> or <i>elephantiasis</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέπρην ἢ λεύκην ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.138
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λειχῆνες καὶ λέπραι καὶ λεῦκαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Prorrh.</u>
					2.43
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἀλφούς τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					85a
				</span></i>
			; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξάνθημα] ὃ καλεῖται λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					518a13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				891a26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>white poplar, Populus alba</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				1.10.1
			</span></i>, al.; used for chaplets, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1007
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				14.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.260
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				2.121
			</span></i>; later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεύκη λευκή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hippiatr.</u>
					22
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> a place at
			Athens where the taxes were let out to farmers of the revenue, prob.
			so called from a <i>poplar</i> in the place, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.133
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρόσακες</span>
			, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				3.133
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> in pl.,
				<i>white spots</i> on the nails, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				1.146
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b> in pl., kind
			of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόγχοι,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδροφυκτίδες</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				42.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>VI.</b> name of
			various plasters, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.414
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>VII.</b>
			<i>white clay</i> or <i>chalk,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
